<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kutama Berbers</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kutama</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kutama were a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> tribal confederation of the mountains of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a>. Converted by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismailism">Ismaili</a> missionary Abu Abdallah al-Shii, they provided the military force that overthrew the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aghlabid-dynasty">Aghlabids</a> and established the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimid Caliphate</a> in 909. Kutama troops remained a core element of the Fatimid army in its early period.</p></div>
